      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fixed for errors, and the header now states the limit for parameters and ports. On PS2 the example gives `1` and then `second`, and doesn\u0027t re-enter `(define a …)`. When the first call is outside any `guard`, a later `(guard … (g))` catches the error, and the generator gives eof afterwards. The `guard` also catches `raise-continuable`, though: see the new comment on 138.",
      "parentUuid": "e9a28142_35a1bc8a",
      "revId": "da9acb64fe00b9596e9b9921bb926aaff1a00467",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
